// Expected to fail (WP11, docs/roadmap/llvm-roadmap.md): `bump` is
// @crashfree but not @wrapping, and `s += 1` overflows for the maximum
// i64. The type checker rejects `+ - *` in such a function but lets the
// compound assignment through; `fid run` and the C path panic with
// "Integer overflow on addition". On the machine layer (`fid emit
// --target x86_64-linux|aarch64-linux|riscv64-linux`) the build itself
// fails: the overflow check survives the MIR folds, which
// compiler/nat_ir.fd ng_crashfree_check reports as
// "native backend: @crashfree violated: function 'bump' is @crashfree but
// can panic: Integer overflow on addition ...".

@crashfree
fn bump(x: i64) -> i64 {
    var s: i64 = x;
    s += 1;
    return s;
}

fn main() {
    println(bump(1));
    println(bump(9223372036854775807));
}
